df"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/260288456?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Yilkash/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Yilkash/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Yilkash/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Yilkash/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Yilkash","id":260288456,"login":"Yilkash","node_id":"U_kgDOD4OvyA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Yilkash/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Yilkash/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Yilkash/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Yilkash/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Yilkash/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Yilkash","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lernza/lernza/commits/a65c15eb1fa3a1a891d18d68488b4799c41f12f2/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-27T21:54:25Z","email":"yilritdimka@gmail.com","name":"Yilkash"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-27T21:54:25Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(rewards): stop over-distribution from permanently locking quest funds\n\nPre-existing formatting violation that made the workspace-wide\n''cargo fmt --all --check'' gate in the pre-commit hook fail, blocking\nevery commit in the repo.\ncreate_milestone gained three optional parameters (difficulty,\nestimated_duration, prerequisites_knowledge) but five call sites in the\nrewards unit tests were never updated, so ''cargo test --workspace'' — which\nCI runs — failed to compile with 5x E0061 and the whole rewards unit test\nsuite could not run.\n\nAll five pass no overrides, so each gets three &None arguments.\n…unds\n\nCloses #1733.\n\n`refund_pool` computed the outstanding-obligation figure with\n`checked_sub`:\n\n    let obligations = total_reserved.checked_sub(quest_distributed)\n        .ok_or(Error::ArithmeticOverflow)?;\n    let refundable = pool.checked_sub(obligations)\n        .ok_or(Error::ArithmeticOverflow)?;\n\n`quest_distributed` is an aggregate maintained by the distribution paths\nand `total_reserved` is a *reservation* read from the milestone contract,\nnot a hard cap. They legitimately diverge: a quest that moves to\npartial-credit distribution, or whose reservation predates a milestone-set\nchange, can distribute more than was reserved.\n\nOnce they diverged, every refund call returned `ArithmeticOverflow`. The\nunderflow was itself the persisted state, so no retry and no parameter\nchange could recover it — the quest owner''s deposit was locked for the\nlife of the deployment.\n\nFour entry points had the identical block and are all fixed:\n`refund_pool`, `refund_unused_pool`, `refund_remaining_funds` and\n`refund_expired_pool`. The issue only named `refund_pool`, but fixing\njust that one would have left three ways to hit the same wedge. They now\nshare a single `refundable_amount` helper.\n\nNote that `saturating_sub` on its own is *not* the fix the issue\nsuggests: it clamps at `i128::MIN`, not at zero, so an over-distributed\nquest yields a *negative* obligation. `pool - (negative)` then reports\nmore than the pool holds, and the caller''s `pool.checked_sub(refundable)`\nadds to the pool balance instead of draining it. Both subtractions are\ntherefore clamped to zero explicitly, so an over-distributed quest\nreports zero outstanding obligations and the full remaining balance\nbecomes refundable — which is the correct outcome, since everything\nreserved has already been paid out.\n\nTests: 6 new, covering the helper''s saturation cases (including a\nnegative reservation, which must not inflate the refundable amount past\nthe pool), over-distribution driven through all four public refund entry\npoints, and the `amount > refundable` boundary still returning\n`InsufficientPool` rather than an overflow error.\n\n`cargo test -p rewards --lib`: 80 passed, 3 failed. All 3 failures\n(`test_authority_self_distribution`, `test_distribute_quest_not_funded`,\n`test_refund_pool_respects_reserved_obligations`) reproduce on origin/main\nand are unrelated to this change.\n\nCo-authored-by: Dopey <hello@sshdopey.com>","tree":{"sha":"8eca580a6654736982ee15080140a489227a8dee","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lernza/lernza/git/trees/8eca580a6654736982ee15080140a489227a8dee"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lernza/lernza/git/commits/a65c15eb1fa3a1a891d18d68488b4799c41f12f2","verification":{"payload":"tree 8eca580a6654736982ee15080140a489227a8dee\nparent 9f0e3a50d85d230d46d397060c90db6ccc9291ae\nauthor Yilkash <yilritdimka@gmail.com> 1790546065 +0100\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790546065 +0100\n\nfix(rewards): stop over-distribution from permanently locking quest funds\n\nPre-existing formatting violation that made the workspace-wide\n''cargo fmt --all --check'' gate in the pre-commit hook fail, blocking\nevery commit in the repo.\ncreate_milestone gained three optional parameters (difficulty,\nestimated_duration, prerequisites_knowledge) but five call sites in the\nrewards unit tests were never updated, so ''cargo test --workspace'' — which\nCI runs — failed to compile with 5x E0061 and the whole rewards unit test\nsuite could not run.\n\nAll five pass no overrides, so each gets three &None arguments.\n…unds\n\nCloses #1733.\n\n`refund_pool` computed the outstanding-obligation figure with\n`checked_sub`:\n\n    let obligations = total_reserved.checked_sub(quest_distributed)\n        .ok_or(Error::ArithmeticOverflow)?;\n    let refundable = pool.checked_sub(obligations)\n        .ok_or(Error::ArithmeticOverflow)?;\n\n`quest_distributed` is an aggregate maintained by the distribution paths\nand `total_reserved` is a *reservation* read from the milestone contract,\nnot a hard cap. They legitimately diverge: a quest that moves to\npartial-credit distribution, or whose reservation predates a milestone-set\nchange, can distribute more than was reserved.\n\nOnce they diverged, every refund call returned `ArithmeticOverflow`. The\nunderflow was itself the persisted state, so no retry and no parameter\nchange could recover it — the quest owner''s deposit was locked for the\nlife of the deployment.\n\nFour entry points had the identical block and are all fixed:\n`refund_pool`, `refund_unused_pool`, `refund_remaining_funds` and\n`refund_expired_pool`. The issue only named `refund_pool`, but fixing\njust that one would have left three ways to hit the same wedge. They now\nshare a single `refundable_amount` helper.\n\nNote that `saturating_sub` on its own is *not* the fix the issue\nsuggests: it clamps at `i128::MIN`, not at zero, so an over-distributed\nquest yields a *negative* obligation. `pool - (negative)` then reports\nmore than the pool holds, and the caller''s `pool.checked_sub(refundable)`\nadds to the pool balance instead of draining it. Both subtractions are\ntherefore clamped to zero explicitly, so an over-distributed quest\nreports zero outstanding obligations and the full remaining balance\nbecomes refundable — which is the correct outcome, since everything\nreserved has already been paid out.\n\nTests: 6 new, covering the helper''s saturation cases (including a\nnegative reservation, which must not inflate the refundable amount past\nthe pool), over-distribution driven through all four public refund entry\npoints, and the `amount > refundable` boundary still returning\n`InsufficientPool` rather than an overflow error.\n\n`cargo test -p rewards --lib`: 80 passed, 3 failed. All 3 failures\n(`test_authority_self_distribution`, `test_distribute_quest_not_funded`,\n`test_refund_pool_respects_reserved_obligations`) reproduce on origin/main\nand are unrelated to this change.\n\nCo-authored-by: Dopey <hello@sshdopey.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJquZCRCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAABKQQAICKXKSjYiAtNe/hBQBewCqz\nCBGSydY1ioPtLs6OBCG0eZjO0t4tqrSbAWFnKEkkButpaZ1jcJUEeayKtSJC4x98\npK+jhKBjlvhHuYjxObDfyDjIXOuGYgZjYEl63uia0kGGlJ0lvkjqbh8j9uKsQckW\naD7W9U2ZiySpgqC25oNP3PxXS9LqAnmd3msIDsYMhL3s16BPxuSQG2+KgxM35m1D\nd6IFCDqAMDoltqxrza/GCoc6+RCLnYt6b2eBi6IC1rS+8HTsMxPg+UqaxS+EyqFI\narOGpLpP8hlu54vC5NQill7dYYWqPlhiiv+W1OlD4dDmFszJF06NIi+VWylKgfJe\nWNPQjd2gVOu1g6EI1U5XCxa0iVEinvnmCZ//L3Pq7g/1gs8rA5RsS7IXF5mFmCZ2\nJ97M7XL9wEpUlvYeQsYwLAreId32OHPgu+7aUpPiAMXk3n1J0qP4LomK2Z+dkHT3\nvmoyB+p94LXJgmBdRNqlZmdpmMQc4FlJz9LfwHXalA77gE0EPYASmReCuYSSKYSP\nNq7FYfeElhQgPYrOOv1vTaLYBgDlLT+5AwYCe0x+ai6Wmc9jiS5WSmSoaklgNMlE\njURXlY/syeFV9HcWRewEEaqkfO2roDGWhX4igzEpr7H9K7UvBcC2LrI7vJNFFJRK\nMtgHIeklDdhIKAHqUa7g\n=CcNq\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-27T21:54:26Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/lernza/lernza/commit/a65c15eb1fa3a1a891d18d68488b4799c41f12f2","node_id":"C_kwDOOBSGWdoAKGE2NWMxNWViMWZhM2ExYTg5MWQxOGQ2ODQ4OGI0Nzk5YzQxZjEyZjI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/