,"node_id":"C_kwDOOBSGWdoAKGY3Y2VlYjMwMDhkMDUxNzVkY2I5ZjQ3MWM2YmE2N2U3Yzg2NTIxOTc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/lernza/lernza/commit/f9a38511ffe2a1562049b24823380e30292cf521","sha":"f9a38511ffe2a1562049b24823380e30292cf521","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lernza/lernza/commits/f9a38511ffe2a1562049b24823380e30292cf521"}],"sha":"f7ceeb3008d05175dcb9f471c6ba67e7c8652197","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lernza/lernza/commits/f7ceeb3008d05175dcb9f471c6ba67e7c8652197"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/260288456?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Yilkash/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Yilkash/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Yilkash/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Yilkash/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Yilkash","id":260288456,"login":"Yilkash","node_id":"U_kgDOD4OvyA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Yilkash/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Yilkash/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Yilkash/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Yilkash/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Yilkash/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Yilkash","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lernza/lernza/commits/f9a38511ffe2a1562049b24823380e30292cf521/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-26T22:18:41Z","email":"yilritdimka@gmail.com","name":"Yilkash"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-26T22:18:41Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Test quest TTL boundaries, fix a CategoryExpiry archival bug, and add creator analytics export\n\nResolves the testable parts of #1645, #1647 and #1648. #1646 needs\ninfrastructure this repo does not have; see the PR description.\n\n#1645 — TTL boundary tests\n\ncontracts/quest/tests/ttl_bump.rs was a placeholder asserting `true`.\nReplaced it with 12 behavioural tests. soroban-env-host 22.1.3 exposes no\nruntime TTL read, so each test advances the ledger and checks whether the\nentry is still reachable. The comparison in extend_ttl(THRESHOLD, BUMP) is\ninclusive, so it is pinned from both sides: exactly THRESHOLD remaining\nrenews, one ledger more is a no-op. Also covers writes on the last live\nledger, anchoring a renewal to the ledger that performed it, and a lapsed\ninstance tier refusing a multi-step commit instead of silently reporting\nan empty contract.\n\nWriting these surfaced a real bug. record_category_expiry stored\nDataKey::CategoryExpiry with a bare `set`, which does not move an entry''s\nTTL, so the key kept the network minimum and was archived. Since\nSelf::bump re-reads it on every public-quest read, any get_quest more than\nmin_persistent_entry_ttl after creation failed with\nError(Storage, InternalError), and get_category fell back to a fabricated\n\"now + BUMP\" expiry. The fix adds the bump the function''s own doc comment\nalready promised. 8 of the 12 tests fail without it.\n\n#1647 — stale architecture docs\n\nThe legacy Workspace routing is already gone, but CLAUDE.md still\ndescribed it. Corrected the crate inventory (the `contracts/*` glob picks\nup `completion`, so there are five contracts plus `common`, not four),\ndropped the reference to the deleted lib/mock-data.ts, and marked the\nWorkspace-to-Quest rename complete. pathToPage is now exported so a guard\ntest can assert the old routes stay 404.\n\n#1648 — creator analytics export\n\nAdds date-range filtering, CSV export and a print-to-PDF report to the\nanalytics page. The filter drives the charts and tables as well as the\ndownloads, so what a creator sees is what they export.\n\nPDF goes through the browser print pipeline rather than a bundled\nlibrary: jsPDF and friends are 150-350 KB against the 200 KB script\nbudget in budget.json, whereas the print pipeline renders the recharts\nSVG already on screen at no bundle cost.\n\nCSV lives in lib/analytics-export.ts so the formatting rules are\ntestable. Quest names are user-controlled strings from the ledger, so\nfields are escaped per RFC 4180 and values beginning with = + - @ are\nprefixed with an apostrophe to stop spreadsheet apps evaluating them.\n\nThe contract stores no per-enrollment timestamp — getEnrollees returns\nbare addresses — so a true enrollment time series is not derivable from\nledger state. The export reports enrollments bucketed by quest creation\nmonth and labels it as such.\n\nCo-authored-by: Dopey <hello@sshdopey.com>","tree":{"sha":"36c2d80eb31beffda15782efa494d9068d536917","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lernza/lernza/git/trees/36c2d80eb31beffda15782efa494d9068d536917"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lernza/lernza/git/commits/f9a38511ffe2a1562049b24823380e30292cf521","verification":{"payload":"tree 36c2d80eb31beffda15782efa494d9068d536917\nparent 5fcfa129d580d68d9cd7473a8a3093b910195908\nauthor Yilkash <yilritdimka@gmail.com> 1790461121 +0100\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790461121 +0100\n\nTest quest TTL boundaries, fix a CategoryExpiry archival bug, and add creator analytics export\n\nResolves the testable parts of #1645, #1647 and #1648. #1646 needs\ninfrastructure this repo does not have; see the PR description.\n\n#1645 — TTL boundary tests\n\ncontracts/quest/tests/ttl_bump.rs was a placeholder asserting `true`.\nReplaced it with 12 behavioural tests. soroban-env-host 22.1.3 exposes no\nruntime TTL read, so each test advances the ledger and checks whether the\nentry is still reachable. The comparison in extend_ttl(THRESHOLD, BUMP) is\ninclusive, so it is pinned from both sides: exactly THRESHOLD remaining\nrenews, one ledger more is a no-op. Also covers writes on the last live\nledger, anchoring a renewal to the ledger that performed it, and a lapsed\ninstance tier refusing a multi-step commit instead of silently reporting\nan empty contract.\n\nWriting these surfaced a real bug. record_category_expiry stored\nDataKey::CategoryExpiry with a bare `set`, which does not move an entry''s\nTTL, so the key kept the network minimum and was archived. Since\nSelf::bump re-reads it on every public-quest read, any get_quest more than\nmin_persistent_entry_ttl after creation failed with\nError(Storage, InternalError), and get_category fell back to a fabricated\n\"now + BUMP\" expiry. The fix adds the bump the function''s own doc comment\nalready promised. 8 of the 12 tests fail without it.\n\n#1647 — stale architecture docs\n\nThe legacy Workspace routing is already gone, but CLAUDE.md still\ndescribed it. Corrected the crate inventory (the `contracts/*` glob picks\nup `completion`, so there are five contracts plus `common`, not four),\ndropped the reference to the deleted lib/mock-data.ts, and marked the\nWorkspace-to-Quest rename complete. pathToPage is now exported so a guard\ntest can assert the old routes stay 404.\n\n#1648 — creator analytics export\n\nAdds date-range filtering, CSV export and a print-to-PDF report to the\nanalytics page. The filter drives the charts and tables as well as the\ndownloads, so what a creator sees is what they export.\n\nPDF goes through the browser print pipeline rather than a bundled\nlibrary: jsPDF and friends are 150-350 KB against the 200 KB script\nbudget in budget.json, whereas the print pipeline renders the recharts\nSVG already on screen at no bundle cost.\n\nCSV lives in lib/analytics-export.ts so the formatting rules are\ntestable. Quest names are user-controlled strings from the ledger, so\nfields are escaped per RFC 4180 and values beginning with = + - @ are\nprefixed with an apostrophe to stop spreadsheet apps evaluating them.\n\nThe contract stores no per-enrollment timestamp — getEnrollees returns\nbare addresses — so a true enrollment time series is not derivable from\nledger state. The export reports enrollments bucketed by quest creation\nmonth and labels it as such.\n\nCo-authored-by: Dopey <hello@sshdopey.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJquETBCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAGjYQAHEXcjvIMMazCJBnVnUB/rTx\nm3x3vkL3MLlCXLs5pc3Twufvs9Ak/MyZGxBPU/ijPJJKzuxpGf0v50Rflyb3/1bT\ntjF5nZoqELO/CZoXxC4NnghL0LpTu2Wj/gJN45BaZaw+VXVhom519BebJPTfPB17\njPLmDJ6VfnEHCY8USCcMA4uxVtH14aB9hgi9xIZQxPKqpcFDZHU2FKNf3hytTTOA\nFkA1MdCYNf9Aw5h+FUXQ5yVID6Gjek9G9vMuCDA1MEJ5Ug+fEpkG9vCI1vZ7/BNj\nO3ZPGn0HIRIgBoJLzqqrpeGfZo8W3F0BJphBKsbq2guKVCyPEy/MUynkZagq9WmZ\nbPAdpXOMOOTySs+K6EeThEP2LELdrbcg8xO7igq/iukgCVRGox+aumBSyRBHBWB5\nBxUwUaIzFD+AypD36QoHyr7EkbfBKHLvJjTBTWxD/ZDI90LopPIeqWveLCDBTlfr\nlo0eMtyQv7QkdQ+J1gxXx7jL2sR0uKMXi5389rm1ECgd/t5YvBG8FoDAiYewKs6C\n+CRsIYxUHEfOyG1+xsTxI20WUFbC3A31yQ9OriUjeSQL0rsh7yDbKWTwaDWD8YDT\nNInp0Lo7/pUIOj7+HEtfyQT6S7+If57b1ivoOvFOVm7oPs3uskF90LEqFcIzlH1N\nup1ni/Oknot+GNrPXG8v\n=w9hc\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-26T22:18:42Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/lernza/lernza/commit/f9a38511ffe2a1562049b24823380e30292cf521","node_id":"C_kwDOOBSGWdoAKGY5YTM4NTExZmZlMmExNTYyMDQ5YjI0ODIzMzgwZTMwMjkyY2Y1MjE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/lernza/lernza/commit/5fcfa129d580d68d9cd7473a8a3093b910195908","sha":"5fcfa129d580d68d9cd7473a8a3093b910195908","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lernza/lernza/commits/5fcfa129d580d68d9cd7473a8a3093b910195908"}],"sha":"f9a38511ffe2a1562049b24823380e30292cf521","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lernza/lernza/commits/f9a38511ffe2a1562049b24823380e30292cf521"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/194638119?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Omoboi-dev/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Omoboi-dev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Omoboi-dev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Omoboi-dev/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Omoboi-dev","id":194638119,"login":"Omoboi-dev","node_id":"U_kgDOC5nxJw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Omoboi-dev/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Omoboi-dev/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Omoboi-dev/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Omoboi-dev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Omoboi-dev/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Omoboi-dev","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lernza/lernza/commits/5fcfa129d580d68d9cd7473a8a3093b910195908/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-26T20:53:34Z","email":"bukunmiabiodun14@gmail.com","name":"Omoboi-dev"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-26T20:53:34Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat: certificate sharing, category management, client tests, and draft auto-save \n\n…ft auto-save (#1637, #1638, #1639, #1640)\n\n- #1637: add certificate sharing modal with OpenGraph preview tags, on-chain explorer links, LinkedIn credential import, and embeddable badge\n- #1638: add category management functions (list_categories, category_quest_count, merge_categories, cleanup) to quest contract\n- #1639: expand contract client layer coverage for RPC fallback, timeout handling, idempotency, and error classification\n- #1640: implement quest draft auto-save every 30s, last-saved status indicator, cross-tab conflict detection, and draft recovery\n\nCo-authored-by: Dopey <hello@sshdopey.com>","tree":{"sha":"0f6f02b4126208d3ed4df7601d53c69029ffa219","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lernza/lernza/git/trees/0f6f02b4126208d3ed4df7601d53c69029ffa219"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lernza/lernza/git/commits/5fcfa129d580d68d9cd7473a8a3093b910195908","verification":{"payload":"tree 0f6f02b4126208d3ed4df7601d53c69029ffa219\nparent bab8f507d9fe1c22bf61e8aa4b2b2682b5e5e970\nauthor Omoboi-dev <bukunmiabiodun14@gmail.com> 1790456014 +0100\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790456014 +0100\n\nfeat: certificate sharing, category management, client tests, and draft auto-save \n\n…ft auto-save (#1637, #1638, #1639, #1640)\n\n- #1637: add certificate sharing modal with OpenGraph preview tags, on-chain explorer links, LinkedIn credential import, and embeddable badge\n- #1638: add category management functions (list_categories, category_quest_count, merge_categories, cleanup) to quest contract\n- #1639: expand contract client layer coverage for RPC fallback, timeout handling, idempotency, and error classification\n- #1640: implement quest draft auto-save every 30s, last-saved status indicator, cross-tab conflict detection, and draft recovery\n\nCo-authored-by: Dopey <hello@sshdopey.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJquDDOCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAC0wQALAI+dc3EHS3Gbvyz0AhzZTn\n9O+qo2P/UjNpLYQxbJDSi8YI+GBvPdyappwPr4CjIFvFXWCCOMX/qJ3NyJOEcgTY\nY2VJc0BuaL15n+SuXu98b24HBqq1MVoypoJFtTggJ/