ff0fbc46a1bc87f7705a","node_id":"C_kwDOOBSGWdoAKDU1ZTUyMDZmYjU2ZDljYzYxNmFlZmYwZmJjNDZhMWJjODdmNzcwNWE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/lernza/lernza/commit/308b869a61f0823da71084071ce448fb1aa26536","sha":"308b869a61f0823da71084071ce448fb1aa26536","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lernza/lernza/commits/308b869a61f0823da71084071ce448fb1aa26536"}],"sha":"55e5206fb56d9cc616aeff0fbc46a1bc87f7705a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lernza/lernza/commits/55e5206fb56d9cc616aeff0fbc46a1bc87f7705a"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/332103760?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Toluwalase-Daniel/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Toluwalase-Daniel/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Toluwalase-Daniel/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Toluwalase-Daniel/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Toluwalase-Daniel","id":332103760,"login":"Toluwalase-Daniel","node_id":"U_kgDOE8uAUA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Toluwalase-Daniel/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Toluwalase-Daniel/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Toluwalase-Daniel/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Toluwalase-Daniel/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Toluwalase-Daniel/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Toluwalase-Daniel","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lernza/lernza/commits/308b869a61f0823da71084071ce448fb1aa26536/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-25T20:30:35Z","email":"toluwalasedaniel4599@gmail.com","name":"Toluwalase-Daniel"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-25T20:30:35Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Real-time events, centralized quest status, wallet error recovery, per-milestone deadlines\n\n… in the quest event stream\n\nuse-quest-events.ts (issue #1628) already polled and parsed a subset of\ncontract events, but silently dropped several real events the milestone\ncontract already emits: milestone_partial, pending_reward_released,\ncertificate_mint_failed, milestone_feedback, dispute_initiated, and\ndispute_resolved. Adds parsing, cache invalidation coverage, and toast/\nnotification handling for all six so quest pages get live updates for\nthe full verification and reward-distribution lifecycle, not just\nhappy-path completion.\nQuest status (active/expired/archived/cancelled) was independently\nrederived in quest-status-badge-helpers.ts, dashboard.tsx, and\nanalytics.tsx, each with subtly different edge cases (a `<` vs `<=`\ndeadline comparison, missing pool-balance checks, hardcoded status\nnumbers). Adds getQuestLifecycleStatus() to lib/utils.ts as the single\nsource of truth. Part of #1629.\n…unction\n\nPart of #1629.\n…al Upcoming bucket\n\ndashboard.tsx''s local deriveQuestStatus() used `deadline < nowSeconds`\n(not `<=`) and routed almost every non-archived/cancelled quest —\nincluding currently-active ones — into an \"upcoming\" bucket that had no\nreal start-time data behind it (QuestInfo has no start-time field), so\nthe Upcoming filter chip could never show what it claimed to. Now\nderives status via the shared getQuestLifecycleStatus() and removes the\ndead Upcoming option. Part of #1629.\nanalytics.tsx counted a quest as \"active\" purely from its on-chain\nstatus enum, so a quest whose deadline had passed but was never\nexplicitly archived was miscounted as still active. Part of #1629.\nWalletErrorAlert showed the raw error message and a single generic\nretry/install button with no guidance on how to actually resolve each\nfailure mode (timeout, rejection, missing API, unknown). Adds ordered\nrecovery steps per WalletErrorCode and an exponential backoff (1.5s,\n3s, 6s, ... capped at 30s) on the retry button so rapid re-clicking\ncan''t hammer Freighter. Part of #1651.\nAdds an optional `deadline` field to MilestoneInfo and a new\nset_milestone_deadline(owner, quest_id, milestone_id, deadline) entry\npoint (owner-only) that validates the milestone deadline doesn''t exceed\nthe quest''s own deadline. Implemented as a separate setter rather than\nextending create_milestone/create_milestone_with_prereqs/\ncreate_milestones_batch''s signatures, to avoid breaking the ~70\nexisting call sites across the contract test suite. submit_for_review\nnow also enforces the milestone''s own deadline, in addition to the\nexisting quest-level deadline check. Resolves #1652.\nAdds `deadline` to the frontend MilestoneInfo type, decodes it from the\ncontract''s MilestoneInfo record, adds setMilestoneDeadline() to call the\nnew contract entry point, and maps the new contract error code\n(MilestoneDeadlineExceedsQuest) to a friendly message. Part of #1652.\nMilestonesSection now renders a countdown badge (turning warning/\ndestructive as the deadline nears/passes) for any milestone that has\nits own deadline set, ticking every 30s. Closes #1652.\n\nCo-authored-by: Dopey <hello@sshdopey.com>","tree":{"sha":"cb2585debe42315ca6a0cbb44b38392a0d463497","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lernza/lernza/git/trees/cb2585debe42315ca6a0cbb44b38392a0d463497"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lernza/lernza/git/commits/308b869a61f0823da71084071ce448fb1aa26536","verification":{"payload":"tree cb2585debe42315ca6a0cbb44b38392a0d463497\nparent 258dae06a16610b1cb23688d0383939cf0d6bc50\nauthor Toluwalase-Daniel <toluwalasedaniel4599@gmail.com> 1790368235 +0100\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790368235 +0100\n\nReal-time events, centralized quest status, wallet error recovery, per-milestone deadlines\n\n… in the quest event stream\n\nuse-quest-events.ts (issue #1628) already polled and parsed a subset of\ncontract events, but silently dropped several real events the milestone\ncontract already emits: milestone_partial, pending_reward_released,\ncertificate_mint_failed, milestone_feedback, dispute_initiated, and\ndispute_resolved. Adds parsing, cache invalidation coverage, and toast/\nnotification handling for all six so quest pages get live updates for\nthe full verification and reward-distribution lifecycle, not just\nhappy-path completion.\nQuest status (active/expired/archived/cancelled) was independently\nrederived in quest-status-badge-helpers.ts, dashboard.tsx, and\nanalytics.tsx, each with subtly different edge cases (a `<` vs `<=`\ndeadline comparison, missing pool-balance checks, hardcoded status\nnumbers). Adds getQuestLifecycleStatus() to lib/utils.ts as the single\nsource of truth. Part of #1629.\n…unction\n\nPart of #1629.\n…al Upcoming bucket\n\ndashboard.tsx''s local deriveQuestStatus() used `deadline < nowSeconds`\n(not `<=`) and routed almost every non-archived/cancelled quest —\nincluding currently-active ones — into an \"upcoming\" bucket that had no\nreal start-time data behind it (QuestInfo has no start-time field), so\nthe Upcoming filter chip could never show what it claimed to. Now\nderives status via the shared getQuestLifecycleStatus() and removes the\ndead Upcoming option. Part of #1629.\nanalytics.tsx counted a quest as \"active\" purely from its on-chain\nstatus enum, so a quest whose deadline had passed but was never\nexplicitly archived was miscounted as still active. Part of #1629.\nWalletErrorAlert showed the raw error message and a single generic\nretry/install button with no guidance on how to actually resolve each\nfailure mode (timeout, rejection, missing API, unknown). Adds ordered\nrecovery steps per WalletErrorCode and an exponential backoff (1.5s,\n3s, 6s, ... capped at 30s) on the retry button so rapid re-clicking\ncan''t hammer Freighter. Part of #1651.\nAdds an optional `deadline` field to MilestoneInfo and a new\nset_milestone_deadline(owner, quest_id, milestone_id, deadline) entry\npoint (owner-only) that validates the milestone deadline doesn''t exceed\nthe quest''s own deadline. Implemented as a separate setter rather than\nextending create_milestone/create_milestone_with_prereqs/\ncreate_milestones_batch''s signatures, to avoid breaking the ~70\nexisting call sites across the contract test suite. submit_for_review\nnow also enforces the milestone''s own deadline, in addition to the\nexisting quest-level deadline check. Resolves #1652.\nAdds `deadline` to the frontend MilestoneInfo type, decodes it from the\ncontract''s MilestoneInfo record, adds setMilestoneDeadline() to call the\nnew contract entry point, and maps the new contract error code\n(MilestoneDeadlineExceedsQuest) to a friendly message. Part of #1652.\nMilestonesSection now renders a countdown badge (turning warning/\ndestructive as the deadline nears/passes) for any milestone that has\nits own deadline set, ticking every 30s. Closes #1652.\n\nCo-authored-by: Dopey <hello@sshdopey.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqttnrCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA2XoQAF4QJGRV3yAToysBVxHnzVsI\nA9Fc0PhxFQKcdHUrWidDHjHB7Sn5QlB7fcuRLmdxhClpFeMEaS+kTzZfypuEtaj0\npQlOtgRK5eFluBRZ0KU+P12GiqeJrXUQZrg8SJj9AnFJez6hTug72UwqflQM3hUd\nfMBi/Iig6NvGVqeZ2W1oR64QPJdUH7YDuU5VChqcIgiIfCCRnieiW7V1SoafHW6Q\npqnigBEjvBuKxkKGBnJYefiQl6n3hE2kv6Sdedhm3bRgNp1Z9YdmXNNM7bDY0rQt\noSZNdwgBzaCuMjsmms2BDrlMHzvhWRrIuG8UHOBGF3oBI/w8QYSp5h+lC9YgK8Up\nBBXypLOyOMw3/Uir9JqKx4t+viDZFUXLn2lZbEfFpCI97SfG3Mq1750WkXEpYUyD\nDTPYv8fha6vl22TTe1PM2GbeHSrCLxEFDerK6OHH3xOKd18ImRpLigXMadcf7mq4\nrrjOTJG90h2idgQYr+ZNARfO0q8rI3vEEhcwaBLNcZceF+lnTEldIjLqu4CK8HYN\nJgcF3MYlfrF0Z+nE0QfxpgLLxfiQQ+SSqsFmTFYI2aMHab4vzi/jOjlKVFZI4eTo\nlK8Sb8tSvkEUhJtNUlPtKCn6WJMwT2QILxQMcWgi3/J2Q3pfKBSQPYGRxb/ZsvQw\nT9hwZuGTw5RfGiiVBWko\n=w7Po\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-25T20:30:35Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":