e,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/lernza/lernza/commit/72523a939260299aaeff6dc57ab536d8f775201d","node_id":"C_kwDOOBSGWdoAKDcyNTIzYTkzOTI2MDI5OWFhZWZmNmRjNTdhYjUzNmQ4Zjc3NTIwMWQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/lernza/lernza/commit/d63910e5cbbf48968193bc15824e3a44f7728f2c","sha":"d63910e5cbbf48968193bc15824e3a44f7728f2c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lernza/lernza/commits/d63910e5cbbf48968193bc15824e3a44f7728f2c"}],"sha":"72523a939260299aaeff6dc57ab536d8f775201d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lernza/lernza/commits/72523a939260299aaeff6dc57ab536d8f775201d"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/308137662?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chikawobishie-sketch/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chikawobishie-sketch/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chikawobishie-sketch/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chikawobishie-sketch/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/chikawobishie-sketch","id":308137662,"login":"chikawobishie-sketch","node_id":"U_kgDOEl3Ovg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chikawobishie-sketch/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chikawobishie-sketch/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chikawobishie-sketch/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chikawobishie-sketch/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chikawobishie-sketch/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/chikawobishie-sketch","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lernza/lernza/commits/d63910e5cbbf48968193bc15824e3a44f7728f2c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-30T16:36:31Z","email":"chikawobishie@gmail.com","name":"chikawobishie-sketch"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-30T16:36:31Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(frontend): standardize deadline utilities on whole seconds\n\nDeadline helpers in utils.ts compared contract timestamps (whole\nseconds) against Date.now() milliseconds via floating-point division\n(nowMs / 1000). The imprecise division and mixed unit comparison caused\noff-by-one and precision drift near the expiry boundary. Convert nowMs\nto whole seconds once with Math.floor and compare against that, matching\nthe expected behavior in #1282.\n\nAdds a regression test for sub-second precision edge cases.\n\nAlso resolves pre-existing frontend test/build failures surfaced while\nrunning the full CI checks locally:\n\n- share-button.test.tsx: expect the current copy strings (\"Copied to\n  clipboard!\" / \"Unable to copy to clipboard. Please try again.\") that\n  the component has used since the copy-feedback messaging change.\n- leaderboard.test.tsx: query the quests switcher by its tab role\n  instead of button (the component renders a tablist/tab pattern).\n- csv-parser.ts: stop stripping the minus sign from reward amounts so\n  negative rewards fail validation instead of silently becoming\n  positive.\n- client.test.ts: import from \"@stellar/stellar-sdk\" root — the\n  \"/minimal\" export no longer exists in stellar-sdk v16.\n- App.test.tsx: mock use-wallet and add ErrorBoundaryProvider to the\n  error-boundary mock so the skip-link tests no longer hit the Soroban\n  RPC client at module load.\n- scripts/load-config.mjs: fix the YAML parser (nested keys were dropped\n  because lines were trimmed before matching indentation) and map config\n  paths to the exact VITE_* names the frontend consumes, so generated\n  .env.local files pass check-env validation and the build succeeds.\n\nGenerated with Codebuff 🤖\nCo-Authored-By: Codebuff <noreply@codebuff.com>\n\nCo-authored-by: Dopey <hello@sshdopey.com>","tree":{"sha":"0ed7e055d235c5ff12aa0f91b1db035cc81293e2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lernza/lernza/git/trees/0ed7e055d235c5ff12aa0f91b1db035cc81293e2"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lernza/lernza/git/commits/d63910e5cbbf48968193bc15824e3a44f7728f2c","verification":{"payload":"tree 0ed7e055d235c5ff12aa0f91b1db035cc81293e2\nparent 4c1e5150b9c1eed7afcdad8339877b7bf2c39163\nauthor chikawobishie-sketch <chikawobishie@gmail.com> 1788107791 +0100\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788107791 +0100\n\nfix(frontend): standardize deadline utilities on whole seconds\n\nDeadline helpers in utils.ts compared contract timestamps (whole\nseconds) against Date.now() milliseconds via floating-point division\n(nowMs / 1000). The imprecise division and mixed unit comparison caused\noff-by-one and precision drift near the expiry boundary. Convert nowMs\nto whole seconds once with Math.floor and compare against that, matching\nthe expected behavior in #1282.\n\nAdds a regression test for sub-second precision edge cases.\n\nAlso resolves pre-existing frontend test/build failures surfaced while\nrunning the full CI checks locally:\n\n- share-button.test.tsx: expect the current copy strings (\"Copied to\n  clipboard!\" / \"Unable to copy to clipboard. Please try again.\") that\n  the component has used since the copy-feedback messaging change.\n- leaderboard.test.tsx: query the quests switcher by its tab role\n  instead of button (the component renders a tablist/tab pattern).\n- csv-parser.ts: stop stripping the minus sign from reward amounts so\n  negative rewards fail validation instead of silently becoming\n  positive.\n- client.test.ts: import from \"@stellar/stellar-sdk\" root — the\n  \"/minimal\" export no longer exists in stellar-sdk v16.\n- App.test.tsx: mock use-wallet and add ErrorBoundaryProvider to the\n  error-boundary mock so the skip-link tests no longer hit the Soroban\n  RPC client at module load.\n- scripts/load-config.mjs: fix the YAML parser (nested keys were dropped\n  because lines were trimmed before matching indentation) and map config\n  paths to the exact VITE_* names the frontend consumes, so generated\n  .env.local files pass check-env validation and the build succeeds.\n\nGenerated with Codebuff 🤖\nCo-Authored-By: Codebuff <noreply@codebuff.com>\n\nCo-authored-by: Dopey <hello@sshdopey.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqlFwPCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAY7EQAHrJBCnyorDUqIea3Tjzhj7g\nFSZtJi7EExhLCEHxevGKSgdHLnzKXZmyMq7j5Qxc01F3WuzppoN9OWh0jQSte716\nG2bBnagSWUIkfJLO37z9f8y7LG2Su+jyvacuDwhuuibBWUw9nZD+anj2FzEXrMgn\nhbE47dt70SY+1lFeD+5WVeBshG1JJUuXwmsspJe2EVYy0vJRxf8wGUciZ7pDf3a5\n1fmM86ioZyZxTVhQswxXv3YzTqqauEqIb/EiDlFrSacqS27ZIgaC8Lq4XKZdmyDT\n+snGfZ5Cx7DIwc7yR488wr3WN2dYiPoe15imQU0wUoaaqkrp+1rxK/tF42CYdxh4\nuEhp9RZ9flqdDDK0RLpetxnvyybBuEzs3iZd8TxOlAnUJd7T6aXBwoUbzepB1FVv\nj2jOZDXls8SEaHS4qgE29qgWOZJSwcjw4tk4ZzBIH4avWK1KssJG3WUR0llgBlPs\n3Z2SFVFhYF6EEdXphNgMKiDPaseUDg44qM/FdYmI0rPJqll+nQIMqCUbwgIaQtvb\nxO4HhxmT0dZ8r9dqHc+Txwzd6aztFvQuebSeo0riyuvcf3h8G+OXQK5KlowzJ1Pq\n0ntKf1TxpgRmITTIEv6I7plIq/cYbuc5XNIOyycnGwjTeY+BnW6iWQOfJJqyVnG7\nIHboFtEcfZn17JckloK2\n=Yz6B\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-30T16:36:31Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/lernza/lernza/commit/d63910e5cbbf48968193bc15824e3a44f7728f2c","node_id":"C_kwDOOBSGWdoAKGQ2MzkxMGU1Y2JiZjQ4OTY4MTkzYmMxNTgyNGUzYTQ0Zjc3MjhmMmM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/lernza/lernza/commit/4c1e5150b9c1eed7afcdad8339877b7bf2c39163","sha":"4c1e5150b9c1eed7afcdad8339877b7bf2c39163","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lernza/lernza/commits/4c1e5150b9c1eed7afcdad8339877b7bf2c39163"}],"sha":"d63910e5cbbf48968193bc15824e3a44f7728f2c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lernza/lernza/commits/d63910e5cbbf48968193bc15824e3a44f7728f2c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/252592806?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dorismaduegbunam/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dorismaduegbunam/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dorismaduegbunam/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dorismaduegbunam/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/dorismaduegbunam","id":252592806,"login":"dorismaduegbunam","node_id":"U_kgDODw5Cpg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dorismaduegbunam/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dorismaduegbunam/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dorismaduegbunam/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dorismaduegbunam/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dorismaduegbunam/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dorismaduegbunam","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lernza/lernza/commits/4c1e5150b9c1eed7afcdad8339877b7bf2c39163/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-29T17:14:39Z","email":"dorismaduegbunam@gmail.com","name":"Innocent Madu"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-29T17:14:39Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat: add cross-contract quest completion flow, certificate page, and Playwright E2E\n\n…ases\n\nAdd edge-case tests for competitive distribution with more completers than\nwinner slots, custom reward amounts exceeding the maximum, peer-review\nverification with insufficient reviewers, milestone submission after quest\nexpiry, and invalid batch milestone ordering. Also repair the existing test\nsuite to compile against the extended create_milestone / MilestoneInput\nsignatures (add the three new optional fields and fix a wrong method name).\nInclude milestone_count in CertificateMetadata, fetched cross-contract from the milestone contract at mint time, and surface it in the frontend certificate client and a new public /certificate/:id page with a shareable template, social sharing, copy-link, and downloadable image.\n… flow\n\nIntroduce a new CompletionContract facade that finalizes a learner''s quest in a single call. It verifies the caller is the quest owner via the quest contract, confirms every milestone is completed by the recipient via the milestone contract, and obtains or mints the on-chain certificate via the certificate contract. Reward distribution for individual milestones remains handled by the milestone contract''s verify_completion, so the facade centralizes the cross-contract checks and certificate finalization that previously had to be orchestrated by the frontend. Includes unit tests exercising ownership, milestone-completion, and double-completion guards.\nAdd a Playwright CI workflow that installs Chromium and runs ''pnpm test:e2e'' against a spawned Vite dev server on pull requests and pushes to main. Also add a certificate page E2E spec covering the new public /certificate/:id route (availability state and client-side routing for arbitrary ids), rounding out coverage of critical user flows.\n\nCo-authored-by: Dopey <hello@sshdopey.com>","tree":{"sha":"170cdfcefee408d31f6cb73bbf61d683fd836582","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lernza/lernza/git/trees/170cdfcefee408d31f6cb73bbf61d683fd836582"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lernza/lernza/git/commits/4c1e5150b9c1eed7afcdad8339877b7bf2c39163","verification":{"payload":"tree 170cdfcefee408d31f6cb73bbf61d683fd836582\nparent 8779d7421383bcc4214f908906348592b8360f54\nauthor Innocent Madu <dorismaduegbunam@gmail.com> 1788023679 +0100\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788023679 +0100\n\nfeat: add cross-contract quest completion flow, certificate page, and Playwright E2E\n\n…ases\n\nAdd edge-case tests for competitive distribution with more completers than\nwinner slots, custom reward amounts exceeding the maximum, peer-review\nverification with insufficient reviewers, milestone submission after quest\nexpiry, and invalid batch milestone ordering. Also repair the existing test\nsuite to compile against the extended create_milestone / MilestoneInput\nsignatures (add the three new optional fields and fix a wrong method name).\nInclude milestone_count in CertificateMetadata, fetched cross-contract from the milestone contract at mint time, and surface it in the frontend certificate client and a new public /certificate/:id page with a shareable template, social sharing, copy-link, and downloadable image.\n… flow\n\nIntroduce a new CompletionContract facade that finalizes a learner''s quest in a single call. It verifies the caller is the quest owner via the quest contract, confirms every milestone is completed by the recipient via the milestone contract, and obtains or mints the on-chain certificate via the certificate contract. Reward distribution for individual milestones remains handled by the milestone contract''s verify_completion, so the facade centralizes the cross-contract checks and certificate finalization that previously had to be orchestrated by the frontend. Includes unit tests exercising ownership, milestone-completion, and double-completion guards.\nAdd a Playwright CI workflow that installs Chromium and runs ''pnpm test:e2e'' against a spawned Vite dev server on pull requests and pushes to main. Also add a certificate page E2E spec covering the new public /certificate/:id route (availability state and client-side routing for arbitrary ids), rounding out coverage of critical user flows.\n\nCo-authored-by: Dopey <hello@sshdopey.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqkxN/CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAcvEQAIKsveMa1k1c+Jx/XlGLg/kw\nzRmiFWnIy1v0IJDiBCTMxS51WpuC/R02apeHH7L3K7yJ8IMv0ALwu75JPv+YCJu9\nVUQ7InEHg/MEzDLr3pOLT+JqghKzuTHYzHn4TTwNvEndKlzxXxQ1DWAao+Z8rBuG\nAPbye9vyOL+YfmnAqg61RdEP0TT9nTifQohWUy1FS15iyvSrNP05WR6NgtgJxoUc\nw8wTELjSNhHDleH+f3ztJQv0ggQ9U0WQrRjzWwPsYiPuA5b8bq5Q9Asjckom9Twm\nMgPi63ETGM4TsWbxly30knw/1tYW4wb36+Sgi5aUVLcd7Od8uBSa2i54zJBWM/83\nVxCdXVcysgjLRXvt7NuGBim0jeebWLWuU8YDAm6GtFI5wUmlAiCH1KuiO8vaI7WI\nxs4ZCAQX/+yM9HJs4onR3oGEPtQT16jbxfO5onTVS+coK5DP2jZIPooqvnsYXhJ6\nESnnD0SxDQQNkcsXuFNQC4ZcYEEi4rWvpSyybhDQ0RHZaq9IS/Qdv4nnFNg+c6cg\npuJvSjC5rjCkv5R4pFjC6C7XDedxksP7kU5wXDZI70x3lRHTDibP1mBgXAneyWjv\nb/c2ReNazQIA3+j9pJQ693SlMlqv1wxK7U+kXD2EBtivHtxlOVqTEpQcH0Mqkh9h\nuqZBuLGF6WWTHg9z3RHl\n=dpih\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-29T17:14:40Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/us