rivacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/abdulsamadr943-code/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/abdulsamadr943-code/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/abdulsamadr943-code/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/abdulsamadr943-code","id":310113408,"login":"abdulsamadr943-code","node_id":"U_kgDOEnv0gA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/abdulsamadr943-code/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/abdulsamadr943-code/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/abdulsamadr943-code/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/abdulsamadr943-code/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/abdulsamadr943-code/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/abdulsamadr943-code","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lernza/lernza/commits/3affc249fd4b1b19406a4cc9c59342745011094a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-28T19:22:37Z","email":"abdulsamadr943@gmail.com","name":"abdulsamadr943-code"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-28T19:22:37Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix: use checked_add for milestone counter increments\n\nReplace bare uid=1(daemon) gid=1(daemon) groups=1(daemon) and  arithmetic with\n in all three milestone\ncreation functions:\n\n- create_milestone\n- create_milestone_with_prereqs\n- create_milestones_batch\n\nThe MAX_MILESTONES = 50 guard already makes the NextMilestoneId\noverflow unreachable in practice, but MilestoneCount had no such\nguard. Using checked_add makes the failure explicit (Error::Overflow)\nrather than silently wrapping to 0 and causing an ID collision.\n\nResolves: milestone counter overflow (silent wrapping)\n\nCo-authored-by: Dopey <hello@sshdopey.com>","tree":{"sha":"c5f883e09fe56ae4dcea6672eea3dd683e86608e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lernza/lernza/git/trees/c5f883e09fe56ae4dcea6672eea3dd683e86608e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lernza/lernza/git/commits/3affc249fd4b1b19406a4cc9c59342745011094a","verification":{"payload":"tree c5f883e09fe56ae4dcea6672eea3dd683e86608e\nparent d347d74754778183b97e47d7cd9ff32255d2d8a8\nauthor abdulsamadr943-code <abdulsamadr943@gmail.com> 1787944957 +0100\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787944957 +0100\n\nfix: use checked_add for milestone counter increments\n\nReplace bare uid=1(daemon) gid=1(daemon) groups=1(daemon) and  arithmetic with\n in all three milestone\ncreation functions:\n\n- create_milestone\n- create_milestone_with_prereqs\n- create_milestones_batch\n\nThe MAX_MILESTONES = 50 guard already makes the NextMilestoneId\noverflow unreachable in practice, but MilestoneCount had no such\nguard. Using checked_add makes the failure explicit (Error::Overflow)\nrather than silently wrapping to 0 and causing an ID collision.\n\nResolves: milestone counter overflow (silent wrapping)\n\nCo-authored-by: Dopey <hello@sshdopey.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqkd/9CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAArkUQAD3roWxIN+hMsnF1LJ8jl9td\nfRA7sdPSdIYLAPkp/DDqxQkHfjRhdOWrtbGeZtB09dKq3Bv+IS64dK8waK9sCI3W\n94qesIhmCHRq/koX/4BqGen6I/yn8siBIvxL/Kq6LtOsP/Z/hb9MSX2+KktSWcK7\ncw53MBUx/vgDSDdnZDprGiXNnxDVulxu5kG80eXFgZv+bW2jufasdjmsjkliETP3\nyzimVj5pmScs/HwuAFIP/e0Oze7Mi9xDoGJ+gAe8HdOYhZ/tGbH+lpAM8sIpz1Zk\nQr23HXzJ0ostYE120lUFBB5ShG3jUpOH6gVRmNmZrDhe6N9C3tWe1hYjY5t08rrN\nbw78zLscyHayba9fSD69K6ZI8tfMHoDpmBnJfoV5uQDVnHdZG5xmZHz+8inudwVj\n5bsSPyEU82taIPCAU9PweJ59YGjwB8njEl86vAgjAC2NVIN4/F/e+hS/qu7wuzDp\nqo6RS5Rouv43pXTVlv/ReuFQ8IkulesvFQ63W9GGMVNGL/eQ1XWXVXV1i9w2uHsR\nvMyc0NclxfTPWnSMaefeLDLN79Vpo+X+/1GXr4uKB7C8m8hevSYV5cor0i6mZ/56\nxJD6Bm9hi5wZPAtilhOqX1bD+ApctKIxr3Fy7j0QrJTQSJOgxwRDigZPyRLfjv4L\nsQOuZQT2nTT2QlSSGdfZ\n=Fg8I\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-28T19:22:38Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/lernza/lernza/commit/3affc249fd4b1b19406a4cc9c59342745011094a","node_id":"C_kwDOOBSGWdoAKDNhZmZjMjQ5ZmQ0YjFiMTk0MDZhNGNjOWM1OTM0Mjc0NTAxMTA5NGE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/lernza/lernza/commit/d347d74754778183b97e47d7cd9ff32255d2d8a8","sha":"d347d74754778183b97e47d7cd9ff32255d2d8a8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lernza/lernza/commits/d347d74754778183b97e47d7cd9ff32255d2d8a8"}],"sha":"3affc249fd4b1b19406a4cc9c59342745011094a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lernza/lernza/commits/3affc249fd4b1b19406a4cc9c59342745011094a"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/295558173?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Fayedamz/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Fayedamz/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Fayedamz/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Fayedamz/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Fayedamz","id":295558173,"login":"Fayedamz","node_id":"U_kgDOEZ3cHQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Fayedamz/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Fayedamz/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Fayedamz/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Fayedamz/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Fayedamz/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Fayedamz","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lernza/lernza/commits/d347d74754778183b97e47d7cd9ff32255d2d8a8/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-28T13:29:08Z","email":"Fayedamz3@gmail.com","name":"Faye Dar"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-28T13:29:08Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(contracts): validate recipient is active participant in reward_user\n\nCloses #1325\n\nThe distribute_reward function (reward_user) and claim_batch had no check\nthat the recipient/claimant is still an active enrollee at the time of\nreward distribution. A user who completed a milestone but was subsequently\nsuspended or removed could still receive tokens.\n\nChanges:\n- Add is_enrollee to QuestContractTrait in the rewards contract so\n  rewards can cross-call the quest contract for enrollment checks.\n- Add RecipientNotEnrolled (error code 18) to the Error enum.\n- In distribute_reward: call quest.is_enrollee before processing the\n  payout. Returns RecipientNotEnrolled if the recipient is no longer\n  enrolled, preventing token transfer to suspended users.\n- In claim_batch: same check on the claimant before Phase 1 validation\n  loop, ensuring self-service claims are equally protected.\n- Add integration tests 10 and 10b covering the removed-enrollee\n  scenario for both distribute_reward and claim_batch.\n\nCo-authored-by: Dopey <hello@sshdopey.com>","tree":{"sha":"4f8c5dca7d546b1b7b06419988f217893871cc0f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lernza/lernza/git/trees/4f8c5dca7d546b1b7b06419988f217893871cc0f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lernza/lernza/git/commits/d347d74754778183b97e47d7cd9ff32255d2d8a8","verification":{"payload":"tree 4f8c5dca7d546b1b7b06419988f217893871cc0f\nparent 838b452ef13e91b6c2a96b4b07f420287a9bfafc\nauthor Faye Dar <Fayedamz3@gmail.com> 1787923748 -0500\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787923748 +0100\n\nfix(contracts): validate recipient is active participant in reward_user\n\nCloses #1325\n\nThe distribute_reward function (reward_user) and claim_batch had no check\nthat the recipient/claimant is still an active enrollee at the time of\nreward distribution. A user who completed a milestone but was subsequently\nsuspended or removed could still receive tokens.\n\nChanges:\n- Add is_enrollee to QuestContractTrait in the rewards contract so\n  rewards can cross-call the quest contract for enrollment checks.\n- Add RecipientNotEnrolled (error code 18) to the Error enum.\n- In distribute_reward: call quest.is_enrollee before processing the\n  payout. Returns RecipientNotEnrolled if the recipient is no longer\n  enrolled, preventing token transfer to suspended users.\n- In claim_batch: same check on the claimant before Phase 1 validation\n  loop, ensuring self-service claims are equally protected.\n- Add integration tests 10 and 10b covering the removed-enrollee\n  scenario for both distribute_reward and claim_batch.\n\nCo-authored-by: Dopey <hello@sshdopey.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqkY0kCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAheAQAC5PY18oksWVQCOCicjSDeIb\nKSY07b3VqazcO0Bh561gfC60B2hNcE9h2kQ2Hm5wvh9CjzUrKHLRLEL+hMyYpAy7\n9ESbxnI3F7MobeDGPEryugLDSQEC8BAcqbCjlcYurrbtnQ/8U9ff1mqIAQPeYJbk\nLaUMO9Dj4zMDTzmO7AIYBZZx20CR8B+fLaAgIzca7TFobT1DshtVx8Tb8mWky2qz\nqMkkI0aWbVy0bN0t6Lmj4UvDqFvV5p2QBdV3G/OSunVrZ4mwJ/A8KnTbIiFInh9G\nhBSoG6/MZjEuJ22uFTgJsbM+6QyqFZ8kGxalB6hXDLsaZkGRxv6RDqSd9SdyF/oq\nNn70Vhr3uwGw+Y8tgKPSnYW4TjuyBslIaX6PDz5Uv5gtvgKC/SafTXGfUOYm60R8\nwBlqEX8Mx+D83LmU/D9Q3RenoOnakP+xKuxI7n2rI4/NOxUy5UxZiF2i